                <pb facs="0262" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg168"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115 St 21/358: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-21T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 21—2:38
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>432. Referring to Department’s 360, October 14, have studied documents supplied
                    by Logan and have consulted Wellman. Because of absence of Prime Minister and
                    indisposition of Sir Eyre Crowe, the Foreign Office suggested that I consult
                    Niemeyer in the Treasury. I presented the case fully to him and stated that both
                    my Government and Standard Oil Company would accept the compromise suggested by
                    arbitrators.</p>
                <p>He stated his firm belief that as a matter of principle the agreed arbitration
                    ought to be completed. Although there was further <pb facs="0263" n="169"
                        xml:id="pg169"/> discussion, there was no change of position. He agreed
                    finally to discuss the case within the next few days with Sir John Bradbury, but
                    I incline to the belief that both have their minds made up. Have informed
                    Logan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
